  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Market study nexus water-hydrogen Namibian contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands embassy in Pretoria, South Africa and the Netherlands consulate-general in Cape Town, South Africa, part of the NL-mission network, are committed to partner up with Namibia in accelerating the energy transition to renewable energy sources. This includes the exchange of knowledge, technology and skills between the Netherlands and Namibia and promoting the development of renewable energy infrastructure, particularly in the field of the combi-track &quot;Green Hydrogen&quot; (GH2), its derivatives, as well as applications.The NL-mission network in South Africa aims at facilitating mutually beneficial trade and investment opportunities between Namibia and the Netherlands and contribute to climate mitigation. To this end, focused research into the market and investment opportunities and mobilisation of Dutch businesses and knowledge institutes is needed. The project is a catalyst in the further development of the combi-track GH2 on Namibia.Development of a successful GH2 chain is a priority area in Namibia, both for local use and application, as well as for export to Europe and the Netherlands. The NL-mission network aims to catalyse the development of GH2 in Namibia, as well as to strengthen relations between Dutch and Namibian stakeholders in this field.This proposition should explain how and in which niches of the GH2 value chain, the Netherlands is best suited to partner with South Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
